{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_142836_c5320e", "exit_code": 0, "text": "# Sales Battlecard: Aurora 14 vs Vantage Pro 16\n\n**Positioning Summary**\nThe Aurora 14 is a premium, upgradeable AI workstation that balances extreme portability with future-proof memory capacity for local model workloads. While the Vantage Pro 16 offers a lower entry price and larger screen, Aurora delivers superior long-term value through performance headroom and on-site service.\n\n**3 Aurora Strengths**\n*   **Upgradeable Memory:** Supports up to 128 GB via user-accessible slots, whereas Vantage is limited to 64 GB soldered RAM.\n*   **AI Performance:** Features a 60 TOPS NPU (vs. 40 TOPS) with sufficient memory to run ~30B-parameter open models locally.\n*   **Portability & Service:** Weighs 0.65 kg less than the competitor and includes a standard 3-year on-site warranty versus 1-year mail-in.\n\n**2 Genuine Vantage Strengths**\n*   **Display & GPU VRAM:** Offers a larger 16-inch screen at 165 Hz and 24 GB of GPU memory, which benefits large 3D scenes and visualization.\n*   **Price & Battery:** Starts $300 lower and provides longer rated battery life (13 hours vs. 11 hours video playback).\n\n**Likely Objections & Responses**\n*   **Objection:** \"Vantage is cheaper.\"\n    *   **Response:** The $300 savings comes with soldered memory limits; Aurora's upgradeability prevents costly replacements when your team needs more RAM for larger AI models.\n*   **Objection:** \"We need the bigger screen for design work.\"\n    *   **Response:** The Vantage's 16-inch panel does excel for visualization, but Aurora's 14-inch OLED offers higher resolution (2880 \u00d7 1800) in a significantly lighter chassis for mobile teams.\n*   **Objection:** \"Battery life is critical for our field users.\"\n    *   **Response:** Vantage leads by two hours on video playback tests, though Aurora still delivers up to 11 hours while weighing 0.65 kg less.\n\n**Discovery Question**\n\"Given that analysts expect memory capacity to matter more as teams run larger AI models on-device, what is your three-year plan for local model size and RAM requirements?\"", "tokens": {"input": 4610, "output": 514, "total": 5124, "cache_read": 0, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 9256, "timestamp": 1790803725981}